From 41e69324f77eeda4deb3aeb752b75c0ab7fa8961 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rahul Kumar <rahul.kumar05@st.com>
Date: Mon, 13 May 2024 15:48:10 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: st: add usb2phy support on stm32mp211

Add USB2PHY support on stm32mp211:
- usb2phy1 is dedicated to the usb 2.0 host controller
- usb2phy2 is dedicated to the usb 2.0 otg controller

The USB2PHY is a clock provider. It provides clocks (e.g. 48MHz) to
the controllers, through RCC:
_______________      ____________________      ______________________
| USB2PHY PLL | ---> | RCC clock gating | ---> | EHCI/OHCI , or OTG |
---------------      --------------------      ----------------------
Add the necessary #clock-cells, so the clock can be requested in the
controller nodes. Distinguish OHCI and PLL clocks on stm32mp211, by
using one cell clock bindings. The OHCI clock must be enabled
specifically during resume from low power.

The OTG controller can be wakeup through USB2PHY2. Add the relevant
wakeup interrupt to the PHY. Mark the PHY and the controller as
"wakeup-source".

Change-Id: I2609a49080a72b9ef4f09aae9e29f9d4448c28b2
Signed-off-by: Rahul Kumar <rahul.kumar05@st.com>
Co-developed-by: Fabrice Gasnier <fabrice.gasnier@foss.st.com>
Signed-off-by: Fabrice Gasnier <fabrice.gasnier@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/linux-stm32/+/559878
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Christian BRUEL <christian.bruel@foss.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/st/stm32mp211.dtsi | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/st/stm32mp211.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/st/stm32mp211.dtsi
index e0540d699b59..8b8675e6bef1 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/st/stm32mp211.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/st/stm32mp211.dtsi
@@ -206,6 +206,30 @@ timer {
 		arm,no-tick-in-suspend;
 	};
 
+	usb2_phy1: usb2-phy1 {
+		compatible      = "st,stm32mp21-usb2phy";
+		#phy-cells      = <0>;
+		#clock-cells    = <1>;
+		st,syscfg       = <&syscfg 0x2400>;
+		clocks          = <&rcc CK_KER_USB2PHY1>;
+		clock-names     = "core";
+		resets          = <&rcc USB2PHY1_R>;
+		status          = "disabled";
+	};
+
+	usb2_phy2: usb2-phy2 {
+		compatible      = "st,stm32mp21-usb2phy";
+		#phy-cells      = <0>;
+		#clock-cells    = <1>;
+		st,syscfg       = <&syscfg 0x2800>;
+		clocks          = <&rcc CK_KER_USB2PHY2EN>;
+		clock-names     = "core";
+		resets          = <&rcc USB2PHY2_R>;
+		interrupts-extended = <&exti1 44 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
+		wakeup-source;
+		status          = "disabled";
+	};
+
 	soc@0 {
 		compatible = "simple-bus";
 		ranges = <0x0 0x0 0x0 0x0 0x80000000>;
-- 
